WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.279
So one of the most common debates you'll read
about online, in books, videos, newspapers,

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:10.000
all over the place is are entrepreneurs born,
or are they made?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.150
And who's right?

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.150
This thing gets heated.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.379
You'll sit at tables and you know, everybody's
born as an entrepreneur.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:23.860
Elon Musk was born with SpaceX, PayPal, and
Tesla and John Doe, even though he doesn't

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.210
know what he's thinking about, he can one
day become an entrepreneur.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.970
Hopeful, wishful, they can become one.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.110
You can do it.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.529
There's no way you're only Elon Musk or you're
not.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:33.910
Who's right?

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.760
So I think the first thing we need to do,
I was having dinner this past week, Thanksgiving

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.309
had friends and family over.

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:43.140
And one of the topics that came up was love.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.100
Somebody brought up a question about hey Pat,
what does it take to run a nonprofit organization

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.629
where you're not paying anybody salaries,
for instance, how do you get a volunteer army

00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:53.629
to be excited about it?

00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:55.059
One of the most important things is love.

00:00:55.059 --> 00:00:57.120
I said, "But here's a question.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.170
Let's define love."

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.780
And I asked everybody one by one by one to
give their definition of love.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.120
Watch what happens.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.780
There's 12 people around the table.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:07.090
Do you know how many different definitions
we got?

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.200
We got eight different definitions of what
love is.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.990
Everyone said something different.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.020
Unconditional.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.060
Sacrifice.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.320
Quality time.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.320
Everybody said something different.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.320
Now watch what the problem is here.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.920
This is one of the reasons why relationships
sometimes don't work out.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.060
My meaning of love is different than your
meaning of love.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.259
Then we clash.

00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:24.579
So you say, "You don't love me anymore."

00:01:24.579 --> 00:01:25.579
You don't love me anymore.

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:26.900
I don't love like you do.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:27.979
You don't love like I do.

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:30.229
You don't love me the way I want to be loved.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:36.340
So today we're going to start off by first
defining what it means to become an entrepreneur.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.210
You see, there are a lot of different definitions,
but I wanted to go to the top two sources,

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:43.260
dictionaries, Oxford and Cambridge.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.090
Let's see how they define what it is to become
an entrepreneur.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:51.039
Cambridge: A person who attempts to make a
profit by starting a company or by operating

00:01:51.039 --> 00:01:56.200
alone in the business world, especially when
it involves taking risks.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.329
This is Cambridge.

00:01:57.329 --> 00:01:58.780
Now let's look at Oxford.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:07.630
A person who sets up a business or businesses,
taking on financial risks in the hope of profit.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:08.729
This is what they're saying.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:10.390
The word profit is used.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:13.320
The word risk is used on both definitions.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:17.710
